<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Postabank's pre-tax profit rises in 1996.</title>
<headline>Hungary Postabank's pre-tax profit rises in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>						 1996		 1995</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    3,347	vs    1,253</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			3,165	vs    2,832</p>
<p>    Net sales			    74,342	vs   76,609</p>
<p>    Other revenues		     32,478	vs    2.513</p>
<p>Expenditures on banking</p>
<p>     activity			    49,936	vs   56,457</p>
<p>    Costs of banking activity	17,782	vs   14,639</p>
<p>    Other expenditures		 35,755	vs    6,773</p>
<p>    Profit of banking activity	3,347	vs    1,253</p>
<p>NOTE: The figures are unaudited. Full company name is Postabank es Takarekpenztar Rt. Postabank is a bank. Its largest single shareholders are the social security pension fund (25 pct), Austria's Osterreichische Postsparkasse (10.4 pct) and the social security health care fund (10 pct).</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
